    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, representing our highest-ceiling plays. **Gunnar Henderson** (82.77) benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a favorable matchup against Tong and his 4.59 xERA, while **Kyle Tucker** (79.09) remains an elite start despite facing a southpaw, as his high-skill base projection overrides the minor platoon penalty. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) is arguably the most intriguing play of the day, with a 14% park boost and a 19% boost from opposing pitcher Sugano\u2019s shaky 4.89 xERA, signaling a high-scoring potential that could move the needle in Roto categories.\n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision involved our utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (40.14) barely clung to his starting role. While **Miguel Vargas** possesses a strong .380 xwOBA, he is fighting a significant 19% drag due to the elite skill profile of Williams, G. He remains a marginal start only because our depth is currently decimated by injuries to **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (44.04) and **Wade Meckler** (44.10) are flirting with the \"below floor\" threshold; both are being started primarily for their contributions to our stolen base scarcity needs, despite facing tough pitching environments that suppress their efficiency scores. We continue to monitor the bench\u2014including prospects like **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014to see if any late-breaking lineup changes or weather shifts in secondary games provide a cleaner path to replacing the low-efficiency outcomes expected from our bottom-order bats.",
